# Rabet — environment variables
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file documents every variable the application reads.
#
# Copy it and fill in real values:   cp .env.example .env.local
# Never commit real secrets — .env* files are git-ignored (.env.example is the
# only exception, and it must always contain placeholders).
#
# The values below are REQUIRED for the admin dashboard to be reachable. Until
# they are provisioned the app fails closed: sign-in is refused and every
# dashboard route redirects to /login. See docs/PHASE_02_HANDOFF.md.

# Public app URL — used for absolute links, OAuth redirects and webhook
# registration. Must match the deployed origin.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Phase 02 — admin authentication (REQUIRED in every environment) --------

# Auth.js session secret. Used to encrypt the session JWT; without it Auth.js
# refuses to serve authenticated requests. Generate one with:
#   npx auth secret        (or:  openssl rand -base64 32)
AUTH_SECRET=replace-with-a-generated-secret

# The single administrator's sign-in email. There is exactly one admin and no
# self-registration, so this is how the admin identity is declared.
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com

# An Argon2id PHC hash of the admin's password — NEVER the plaintext password.
# Generate it locally with an interactive prompt (the password is never echoed
# to the terminal, written anywhere, or logged):
#   node scripts/generate-admin-hash.mjs
# Paste the whole `$argon2id$...` string here. A value that is not an Argon2
# PHC string is rejected at startup and sign-in stays disabled.
ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=replace-with-an-argon2id-hash-from-scripts/generate-admin-hash.mjs

# --- Phase 03B — database (OPTIONAL for build; required by the DB layer) -----
# PostgreSQL connection string on Neon. The app builds and serves every current
# route without it; getDb() fails loudly with a credential-free message on first
# use when it is absent. Required to run `npm run db:migrate` / `db:check` and
# by any future route that reads or writes the database.
# Format: postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/DATABASE?sslmode=require
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require

# Telegram bot token issued by @BotFather — Phase 06 (Telegram bot onboarding)
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=0000000000:AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA

# --- Test-only variables (never set in a real deployment) -------------------
# Designates the throwaway PostgreSQL cluster the database integration suites
# create and drop databases on. Never read by the application, and never the
# same value as DATABASE_URL. Locally `npm run test:db` sets it for you; CI
# points it at an isolated service container.
# RABET_TEST_PG_URL=postgresql://rabet@127.0.0.1:PORT/postgres

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No payment variable exists. The MVP has no checkout, no orders and no
# invoices — an inquiry is a conversation, not a purchase (ADR-013). Any future
# in-bot sale is built on compliant Telegram Stars checkout, which needs no
# provider token for digital goods, and is a separately scheduled feature.
